  "id": "contrast-polarity",
  "term": "contrast polarity",
  "definition": "Contrast polarity is a visual feature that describes whether an element differs in luminance from its background in one direction or the opposite direction, often framed as “on” versus “off” polarity. In this source, it is treated as a property that can distinguish visual items, although numerosity judgments in the subitizing range were not found to depend on it.",
